36. VERY IMPORTANT DIFFERENCE
------------------------------------------------------------

top():

    Gives the highest-priority element.


pop():

    Removes the highest-priority element.


Example:

    cout << pq.top();

This only reads.


But:

    pq.pop();

actually removes it.


To read and remove:

    cout << pq.top();
    pq.pop();



37. COMMON MISTAKE
------------------------------------------------------------

