49. HEAP SORT
------------------------------------------------------------

Heap Sort works using a heap.

Basic idea:

    Build Heap

    Repeatedly remove top


Max Heap can produce:

    descending sequence


Min Heap can produce:

    ascending sequence


Complexity:

    O(N log N)



50. BUILD HEAP COMPLEXITY
------------------------------------------------------------

If we build a heap from N elements,
heap construction can be done in:

    O(N)


This is better than inserting N elements
one by one into an initially empty heap:

    O(N log N)


For STL, you usually don't need to implement
heap construction manually.

But the complexity is important to know.



51. HEAP DATA STRUCTURE VS PRIORITY_QUEUE
------------------------------------------------------------

Heap:

    The underlying data structure.


priority_queue:

    C++ STL container adaptor that provides
    priority queue behavior using a heap.

In competitive programming, we usually directly use:

    priority_queue



